                    <ol><li><a href="#Oxidation_of_Alkyl_Side_Chains" rel="internal">Oxidation of Alkyl Side Chains</a></li><li><a href="#" rel="internal">&nbsp;</a></li><li><a href="#Analogous_side-chain_oxidations_occur_in_various_biosynthetic_pathways._The_neurotransmitter_norepinephrine.2C_for_instance.2C_is_biosynthesized_from_dopamine_by_a_benzylic_hydroxylation_reaction._The_process_is_catalyzed_by_the_copper-containing_enzyme_dopamine___-monooxygenase_and_occurs_by_a_radical_mechanism._A_copper.E2.80.93oxygen_species_in_the_enzyme_first_abstracts_the_pro-R_benzylic_hydrogen_to_give_a_radical.2C_and_a_hydroxyl_is_then_transferred_from_copper_to_carbon." rel="internal">Analogous side-chain oxidations occur in various biosynthetic pathways. The neurotransmitter norepinephrine, for instance, is biosynthesized from dopamine by a benzylic hydroxylation reaction. The process is catalyzed by the copper-containing enzyme dopamine   -monooxygenase and occurs by a radical mechanism. A copper&ndash;oxygen species in the enzyme first abstracts the pro-R benzylic hydrogen to give a radical, and a hydroxyl is then transferred from copper to carbon.</a></li><li><a href="#Bromination_of_the_Benzylic_Carbon" rel="internal">Bromination of the Benzylic Carbon</a><ol><li><a href="#NBS_as_a_Bromine_Source" rel="internal">NBS as a Bromine Source</a></li><li><a href="#Allylic_Bromination_Mechanism" rel="internal">Allylic Bromination Mechanism</a></li></ol></li><li><a href="#Acyl_Side_Chain_Reductions" rel="internal">Acyl Side Chain Reductions</a></li><li><a href="#Contributors_and_Attributions" rel="internal">Contributors and Attributions</a></li></ol>
